       has been lifted out of flow, and the grid collapses to the index alone,
       which is exactly what should be behind the sheet.

       ⚠ `visibility` RATHER THAN `display`, so the transform has something to
       animate and the embed keeps its layout box while closed — a `display:
       none` iframe is re-laid-out on every open, which is the flicker the first
       bench spent its whole budget removing. It is also what lets a playing
       embed go on playing behind the index, which the header records as a known
       and accepted cost rather than an oversight. */
    .sets-room > #set-detail {
